# --- Working artefacts and generated deliverables -------------------------------
# Anything left in the deploy root is served as a STATIC file, which bypasses the
# app's Supabase auth gate completely — sales.jmfinancelab.com/<filename> would hand
# out the KAM review (named managers, named accounts, the defection register), the
# driver book and the account-level forecast workbooks to anyone with the URL.
# The app itself needs only JPS_Sales_Platform_v1.html, config.js, jps-monitor.js,
# shared/ and og-image.png, so everything else is excluded by pattern rather than by
# name — a new report dropped in the root next session must not silently ship.
JPS_Exec_Summary*.html
JPS_KAM_Review*.html
JPS_System_Losses*.html
JPS_Sales_Forecast_*
JPS_Forecast_*
JPS_LE_Sales_Gen_*
architecture-map.html
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.docx
*.pdf
*.csv
~$*

# Scratch scripts and solver output (_check_sp.js alone is 595 KB of embedded data).
_*.js
_*.json
_*.txt

# Repo-side only — schema, SQL and instructions have no business being downloadable.
migrations/
supabase/
reports/
